---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Contact" description="Check inquiry availability for Wellridge Group funding and program-operations support.">
  <section class="py-20 bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-6">Contact Wellridge Group</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">
        Inquiry channels for wellridgegroup.com are being prepared. No contact form, email inbox, or scheduling link is active on this site yet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
        <!-- Inquiry Status -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">Inquiry Status</h2>
          <div class="bg-fog p-8 rounded-lg">
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4">
              Contact intake is not yet open. A controlled mailbox and scheduling workflow will be published here after ownership, privacy, and response responsibilities are confirmed.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
              Please do not send confidential, procurement-sensitive, personal, health, or client information through an unverified channel.
            </p>
            <span
              role="status"
              aria-label="Contact channel coming soon"
              class="inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-ridge-blue text-white rounded-md font-medium opacity-70"
            >
              Contact Channel Coming Soon
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Scope Preparation -->
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">Prepare for a Scope Conversation</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">When intake opens, it will help to have:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Your organization and buyer type.</li>
            <li>The funding opportunity or program need.</li>
            <li>A deadline, decision date, or target launch window.</li>
            <li>The specific deliverables you need owned.</li>
            <li>Available source documents and a named decision-maker.</li>
            <li>Any clinical, technical, legal, data, or security boundaries.</li>
          </ul>

          <!-- Mini FAQ -->
          <div class="mt-12">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">Quick Questions</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-deep mb-1">What work is Wellridge preparing to support?</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
                  Two bounded paths: a Nonprofit Funding Pipeline Sprint and Proposal &amp; Program Operations Support for nonprofits, established public-sector contractors, and selected agencies.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-deep mb-1">Does Wellridge guarantee funding or awards?</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
                  No. Opportunity qualification and proposal discipline can improve decision quality, but award decisions remain with the funder or contracting authority.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-deep mb-1">Does Wellridge provide clinical or technical services?</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
                  No. Wellridge may own nonclinical administration, coordination, engagement, compliance, reporting, and closeout; clinical care, engineering, and other specialized judgment stay with appropriately qualified professionals.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-deep mb-1">How is work scoped?</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
                  Work is defined in a fixed-scope or milestone-based statement of work with named deliverables, inputs, approvals, and change control. Compensation is not based on a percentage of an award.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
